Author: missingbulb <73882448+missingbulb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Sep 28 19:48:59 2026 +0300

    Planner: offer every overlapping show, and give untimed shows their hour (#950)

    * Planner: offer every show that overlaps a card, not only same-minute starts

    A drafted card offered as rivals only the shows starting on its exact
    minute, so a festival that staggers its halls a quarter-hour apart (Haifa:
    12:00, 12:15, 12:30) showed almost none of the alternatives it has. A show
    now counts as a rival of the night's card it cannot sit beside, the one it
    overlaps longest.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VeUN3YDBWkwmUhQhTyjAaS

    * Planner: a show with no published length holds its assumed hour

    The draft counted such a show as lasting no time at all, so Haifa's
    19:30 "Shorts from the Past 3" was followed by a 20:00 screening across
    town. Clashes now see it running for the same assumed length the day's
    hours already use; its card still names only its start.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VeUN3YDBWkwmUhQhTyjAaS

    * Refresh the planner goldens for the drafter's rivals and untimed shows

    Contested cards now draw every overlapping rival, and a few drafts move
    where an untimed show holds its hour.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VeUN3YDBWkwmUhQhTyjAaS

